mode: "100644"
text: "# Post types, the commenting playbook + two worked examples\n\n## Native post types (in rough 2026 order of favor)\n| Type | When | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Document/PDF carousel | framework, checklist, breakdown | highest dwell + saves; slides → `carousel-writer`; posted natively |\n| Native video (<90s, captioned) | POV to camera, demo | LinkedIn's current push; → `talking-head-and-piece-to-camera` |\n| Text: story → lesson | something that actually happened | ~1,800–2,100 chars if it earns the read |\n| Text: contrarian POV | a take you'll defend | close on a genuine question, not \"Agree?\" |\n| Text + image | proof, data, before/after | image lifts the stop, text does the work |\n| Newsletter edition | recurring theme, depth | notification + email push; created natively |\n| Poll | a genuinely contested question | engagement yes, follow-conversion weak |\n\n**Link rule:** external links go in the **first comment** (\"link in comments\"), never the body.\n**Cadence:** 3–5/week, max 1/day. Post craft → `linkedin-post-writer`.\n\n## The commenting playbook (the afterburner)\n1. **Build the target list (10–20 accounts):** ~60% bigger voices in your niche, ~30% peers,\n   ~10% dream clients/partners. Turn on the bell for the big ones.\n2. **5–10 substantive comments/day**, ideally within the first hour of their post going live. Each\n   comment adds something: a number from your experience, a respectful counterpoint, a sharper\n   example, a question that extends the idea. 2–4 sentences. Never \"Great post! 🙌\".\n3. Your **headline travels with every comment** — that's the impression it makes. (Fix the headline\n   first: LADDER step L.)\n4. After a few real exchanges, **connect with a no-pitch note** referencing the conversation.\n5. Drafts → `reply-and-comment-writer`; the daily block → `engagement-routine`; **a human posts\n   every comment** — automation risks restriction.\n\n## The golden-hour routine\n15 min before posting: leave 2–3 comments on target accounts → post in the audience window →\nreply to **every** comment for 60–90 min, ending replies on questions to reopen threads → back at\nthe 3-hour mark for stragglers. A strong post keeps resurfacing for days — keep answering.\n\n## Connection-request hygiene\n~100 invites/week max; spend them on people you've already engaged. Note optional when context is\nobvious (they replied to you), otherwise one specific sentence. **Never pitch in the invite or the\nfirst message after accepting** — warm the relationship in public first (→ `social-selling-and-dm`).\n\n## Worked example 1 — consultant with no reach (fix: comments before posts)\n```\nDIAGNOSIS: 2 posts/week into a cold network; headline = \"Managing Director\"; zero commenting.\nPLAN: Headline → \"Pricing strategy for B2B SaaS | I help founders stop discounting\" (profile-optimization).\nCOMMENTS: 12 target accounts (5 big SaaS voices, 5 peers, 2 dream clients); 7/day drafted from\ntheir fresh posts — each adds a pricing data point or counterexample.\nPOSTS: 3/week — Mon carousel (\"The 4 discount traps\"), Wed story→lesson, Fri contrarian POV.\nLinks (case study) in first comment. Golden hour blocked in calendar.\nEXPECT: profile visits + follower growth from week 2-3 via comments; post reach compounds after.\n```\n\n## Worked example 2 — founder launching a newsletter (warm audience, expertise moment)\n```\nTRIGGER: new EU regulation hits their industry (trend-jacking moment).\nPOST (text, no link): \"Everyone's panicking about [regulation]. For companies under 50 people,\nonly one clause actually bites -- here's the two-week fix we're running.\" Ends: \"What's your\ncounsel telling you? Genuinely curious what advice is circulating.\"\nGOLDEN HOUR: founder answers every comment personally; best question becomes Thursday's post.\nFOLLOW-ON: launches the LinkedIn newsletter (\"The [industry] Brief\") on the spike -- LinkedIn\npushes subscribe prompts to the network; the first-comment link points to the lead magnet\n(lead-magnets-and-funnels). Off-platform list mirrored via email-and-newsletter.\n```\n\nBoth: read `brand-profile` + `voice-builder` first; person not page; links in first comment; human\ndoes the live engagement; posts scheduled via `scheduling-and-queue` → WoopSocial; results read from\nnative LinkedIn analytics — never fabricated.\n"
